Id: con019c
Severity: CONFIG
Category: tigris
Check: config
Fix: Nothing, if the directory is yours: a bind mount keeps its owner from the host. Otherwise mount one that is.
References: tigris(8)

The working or log directory belongs to a uid that is not root, the
user running Tigris or the user who invoked sudo, which on a host would
stop the run (con018e: Tigris writes there under names a bystander could
guess and follows a link found in their place). Tigris is running inside
a container, where such a directory is the host user's bind mount and
nobody else runs, so it is used, and this says so.
